3.Analyze Performance Metrics
Samples
The number of requests recorded by JMeter.
Average Response Time
The average time taken to receive responses. Lower response time generally indicates
faster response, subject to application requirements.
Minimum Response Time
The fastest recorded response.
Maximum Response Time
The slowest recorded response. A large difference between average and maximum may
indicate occasional slow responses.
Throughput
Throughput indicates the rate at which requests are processed, commonly displayed by
JMeter as requests per second. It should be considered together with response time
and error percentage.
Error Percentage
Error percentage indicates the percentage of requests that failed.
Formula: Error % = (Failed Requests / Total Requests) × 100
Example: If 5 out of 100 requests fail, Error % = (5 / 100) × 100 = 5%.
